# Every environment variable this workspace reads.
#
# Nothing loads this file. The binaries read the process environment and
# nothing else, so export what you need in your shell. Copying this to `.env`
# is fine for tooling that sources one (git ignores `.env`; this file is the
# one exception), but see the private key below before putting anything else
# in it.

# --- Metadata tier (optional) -----------------------------------------------
#
# Postgres from docker-compose.yml. Unset, or a database that will not answer,
# the recorder logs a warning and records anyway: an index row can be rebuilt
# from the capture and market data cannot. The quant-meta tests skip
# themselves without it.
QUANT_DATABASE_URL=postgres://quant:quant_local_dev@localhost:5432/quant

# --- Live path only (venue-check, live) -------------------------------------
#
# The API key Binance issued for your registered Ed25519 public key.
# BINANCE_API_KEY=
#
# The Ed25519 private key's text, not a path to it. Keep the key file outside
# this repository and load it from there; never paste it into a `.env` here,
# where `.gitignore` would be the only thing between it and a public repo.
#
#   bash:        export BINANCE_ED25519_PRIVATE_KEY="$(cat "$HOME/.binance/ed25519.pem")"
#   PowerShell:  $env:BINANCE_ED25519_PRIVATE_KEY = Get-Content -Raw "$env:USERPROFILE\.binance\ed25519.pem"
#
# `venue-check --help` says how to make the pair. BINANCE_API_SECRET, the HMAC
# secret the live path used before Ed25519, is no longer read for signing.

# --- Logging (record, paper, live, verify) ----------------------------------
#
# A tracing filter. Unset, record, paper and live log at `info` and verify at
# `warn`.
# RUST_LOG=info
